    "created_at": "2016-02-08T01:54:28Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-02-08T01:54:28Z",
    "body": "I'm pretty sure there are existing issues on this (I certainly recall discussion in them), but basically the whole implicitthis thing is silly as defined right now.  It would need to be defined on Window, and also on EventTarget, and various interfaces that Window implements (via \"implements\" statements) and all the interfaces that are on the ancestor chain of the global in workers and anything implemented by any of those.\n\nI _think_ the last time this was discussed the conclusion was basically that the [ImplicitThis] behavior should be the only behavior in IDL.  Then for operations/attributes for which it makes sense (i.e. the ones that expect to get the global as `this`) it would do the right thing, and for other ones you would get an exception, just like you get an exception for `undefined` if none of this [ImplicitThis] stuff is happenign (though UAs should feel free to make the exception as informative as they like, of course).\n\n@domenic, does that correctly reflect the current state of thinking on this stuff?  I can't remember where the discussion about this was....\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
